        "question": "Is an online signature legally valid in India under the IT Act 2000?",
        "answer": "Yes. Under ==Section 5 of the Information Technology Act, 2000==, an electronic signature possesses equal legal standing to a traditional handwritten wet-ink signature, provided it conforms to authentication standards prescribed by the Controller of Certifying Authorities (CCA). For everyday recruitment portals (UPSC, SSC, State PSCs), scanned and resized signature images are legally recognized submissions of candidate identity."
