        "answer": "An online signature (or electronic signature) is any digital sound, symbol, or process attached to a contract with the intent to sign. Under the ==federal ESIGN Act (2000)== and the ==Uniform Electronic Transactions Act (UETA)==, electronic signatures carry the same legal weight and enforceability as handwritten wet-ink signatures across commercial, employment, and real estate contracts in all 50 states."
